      "page_title": "Rc<RefCell<T>>: The Shared-Mutable Combo",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "{",
            "    let mut g = rc.borrow_mut();",
            "    *g += 1;",
            "}   // guard released here"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Temporaries Die At The Semicolon",
          "text": "`*a.borrow_mut() += *b.borrow();` works — both guards drop at statement end. The same line where `a` and `b` are the same cell panics."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Before You Reach For It"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Dense graph? An arena — `Vec<Node>` plus `usize` ids — is faster",
            "`Rc<RefCell<T>>` in a structure means audit for cycles",
            "`type Shared<T> = Rc<RefCell<T>>;` keeps signatures readable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How A Cycle Leaks",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two or more `Rc`s pointing at each other",
            "Each keeps the other's strong count above zero",
            "The count never hits 0, so `drop` never runs",
            "Memory leaks — safe in Rust, still wrong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Safety Is Not Leak-Freedom",
          "text": "Rust guarantees memory safety, not the absence of leaks. `Rc` cycles and `mem::forget` are both perfectly sound."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reproduce It"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let a = Rc::new(RefCell::new(Cons(5, nil)));",
            "let b = Rc::new(RefCell::new(Cons(10, a2)));",
            "*a.borrow_mut().tail() = Rc::clone(&b);",
            "// strong_count(a) = 2 and stays there"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two `Rc<RefCell<Cons>>` nodes, tails set to each other",
            "Print `Rc::strong_count` — it never returns to 0",
            "Printing the list overflows the stack: the loop is real"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
