    {
      "page_title": "Common Mistakes and Gotchas",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The Recursion Trap",
          "text": "A method that borrows and then calls itself borrows twice and panics. Restructure so the guard is passed down instead."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Misread Clones"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`a.clone()` on `Rc<Vec<T>>` clones the pointer",
            "Not the vector — obvious to Rust, surprising in review",
            "`==` on two `Rc`s compares the pointed-to values",
            "`Rc::ptr_eq` is the identity test"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "drop() And get_mut()",
          "items": [
            "`drop(x)` on an `Rc` merely decrements",
            "It frees early only when no clone exists",
            "`Rc::get_mut` returning `None` means still shared",
            "That is a signal, not a bug"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Design Smells"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Rc<RefCell<T>>` where `&mut` plus a restructure would do",
            "It trades compile errors for runtime panics",
            "`Rc<RefCell<Rc<RefCell<..>>>>` — flatten or use an arena",
            "Missing `Weak` back-pointers: the #1 leak source in graphs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Threads And Async"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Rc` across threads never compiles",
            "Swapping in `Arc` blindly hides that you still need a lock",
            "Deadlock: two threads, two mutexes, opposite order",
            "No borrow checker helps you there"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let g = m.lock().unwrap();",
            "do_io().await;   // guard held across await",
            "// std Mutex poisons async code here —",
            "// use tokio::sync::Mutex instead"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Dispatch Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Box<dyn Trait>` pays a vtable hop on every call",
            "In a hot loop that is measurable time",
            "Generics monomorphize — no indirection at all",
            "Choose `dyn` for flexibility, not for speed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Repair Order",
          "text": "Panicking `RefCell`? Shorten the borrow first, restructure the ownership second, move to an arena last."
        },
