  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of RUST SMART POINTERS. Your Rust program can leak memory without a single line of `unsafe` — two `Rc`s pointing at each other, and the count never reaches zero. This handbook walks the whole pointer family: `Box` for one owner on the heap, `Rc`/`Arc` for many, `Cell`/`RefCell`/`Mutex` for mutating through a shared reference, and `Weak` for the back-pointer that breaks the cycle. Ten pages of layouts, costs, panic messages and the decision order worth memorising.",
